cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Vernier-RV32: a pipelined RV32IMA core and Wishbone SoC,
  verified against riscv-tests, Spike and formal methods
message: >-
  If you use this project in academic work, please cite it using
  these metadata. Note that CoreMark figures reported here are
  unverified self-measurements and are not EEMBC-certified scores.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aravind
    family-names: Rajesh Kanna
    alias: AravindRajeshkanna
repository-code: 'https://github.com/AravindRajeshkanna/vernier-rv32'
abstract: >-
  Vernier-RV32 is a five-stage pipelined RISC-V RV32IMA
  implementation with machine, supervisor and user modes, an Sv32
  MMU, a branch target buffer, and a Wishbone B4 system-on-chip
  comprising boot ROM, on-chip RAM, CLINT, PLIC, UART, GPIO, SPI
  and a framebuffer. It is verified in four independent layers:
  directed testbenches, the upstream RISC-V architectural test
  suite, instruction-level co-simulation against the Spike
  reference model, and bounded model checking with Yosys and Z3.
  The design synthesises for the Lattice ECP5 and has been run on
  a ULX3S board, where it boots from a preloaded image and passes
  its acceptance test at 25 MHz.
keywords:
  - risc-v
  - rv32ima
  - cpu
  - soc
  - verilog
  - fpga
  - ecp5
  - ulx3s
  - wishbone
  - formal-verification
  - co-simulation
